## Premises (measured by the feed2 drafter at 22:35:29 AEST, in a `--shared` scratchpad clone detached at 581ed7fa1; Wednesday re-derives before queueing)
- THE DEFECT of `KS-864-R15-F1009.md` (run `runs/2026-09-21_ks864-ornith35b-night`, FAIL T5 "DECLARED CELL NOT IN THE RUN"): both declared titles carried the loop template `${nodeEnv}`; the checker matches the FULL RENDERED title (IMPROVEMENTS 2026-09-21 22:22 rule: declared cell titles are LITERAL rendered strings; a looped cell declares each rendered title or is written as N literal cells). The run itself was green 10/10.
- THE SECOND THING THE TEMPLATE HID: `describeUnder` runs the block TWICE (`'staging'`, `'development'`). Under the tamper `env: 'development'` only the STAGING block's F-1009-2 cell can red (`'development' !== 'staging'`); the DEVELOPMENT block's reads `'development' === 'development'` and stays green. A RED-titled cell that is green under the tamper would fail T6 ("declared but GREEN"), so the development-block cell is written as a CONTROL, by a literal per-block title chosen with a ternary (no template in any declared title).
- Reachability at 581ed7fa1: each block imports a FRESH `routes/system-status` (`vi.resetModules` :54) under its own `NODE_ENV` (:56) and reads GET /api/system/status; the handler builds `environment.env` at system-status.ts:446 `env: process.env.NODE_ENV || 'development'` (exact whole-line match count 1 at the tip). The tamper hard-codes `'development'`; the staging block then serves `env: 'development'` -> its F-1009-2 cell reds by assertion.
- The F-1009-1 edit of the held READY (per-block env VALUES `p.value + '/' + nodeEnv`, so a development block that reads a staging-loaded module reds) is kept byte-for-byte - it is a test-side property, not graded by a tamper, as the 09-17 READY said.
- Ticket KS-864: Backlog; PR attachments #1007, #1009, #1064, #1073 (all merged). Nothing in the product changes.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)
`ks864c-portal-env-vars.test.ts` pins that each portal's env var wins under NODE_ENV=staging and =development, but nothing pins that the served `environment.env` is the block's NODE_ENV (system-status.ts:446), and the two blocks set IDENTICAL portal values so a block that read the OTHER block's module would still be green (F-1009-1). This task is the PIN, test-only: per-block values, plus one F-1009-2 cell per block with a LITERAL title (the staging one reds under the tamper; the development one is a control), plus one control per block that the status body carries an environment block at all.

## THE MODE - read this twice
TEST-ONLY, MODIFY IN PLACE: your diff contains EXACTLY ONE file, the EXISTING test file above, as the THREE hunks below (context lines byte-for-byte from the tip; no blank context line; no blank + line). No product hunk. The hunk headers are `@@ -48,2 +48,7 @@`, `@@ -54,7 +59,8 @@` and `@@ -71,7 +77,15 @@` - copy them.

## The exact change
```
